1. Attach an `onClick` to the overlay so that clicking outside the nav will close it.  
2. Attach an `onClick` to the `<nav>` itself so that clicking any `<a>`–which is how `SideNavLink` renders a React-Router `<Link>`–will also fire the same collapse logic.

Note that in a controlled setup you must also pass your parent’s toggle callback into the `SideNav` as its `onToggle` prop if you want the library to notify you of the collapse; otherwise the collapse will only happen in the library’s internal state.

