With this patch:

- Clicking the gray overlay now invokes `handleToggle(event, false)` to collapse.  
- Clicking any `<a>` inside the nav (i.e. your `SideNavLink` → React-Router `<Link>` → `<a>`) also collapses.  

If you’re controlling `<SideNav>` from the outside via its `expanded` prop, make sure to wire up your parent toggle callback by passing it as `onToggle={onClickSideNavExpand}` so that the library’s internal `handleToggle` will notify you to update your own `isSideNavExpanded` flag.
